      "answer": {
        "ideal": "(a) “The castle frowned” is personification: frowning is a human expression given to the castle, making it seem stern or forbidding.\n\n(b) A chair stands where the castle was, and a carpet covers the place of the garden. The child can no longer find the magic land on waking.\n\n(c) Boots stand by the door instead of horsemen. A bath and water-can take the place of the streams. These are ordinary objects in his waking room."
