    {
      "answer": {
        "ideal": "(a) At bedtime, the child finds pictures of a magic land in his head or imagination and sees them clearly.\n\n(b) “In vain” means without success. The magic land exists in his dream or imagination, so when he wakes he sees his ordinary room instead.\n\n(c) At bedtime the child is excited or delighted by clear pictures of castles, magic gardens and other adventures. In the morning he is disappointed or longs to return, because he searches for the magic land without success and finds familiar objects such as a chair and carpet instead."
